Expected Result:
[BLADE] A second blade opens titled with the fulfillment center's own name (e.g. @td(FC_EAST.name)), carrying a product-count badge {OBSERVED}
[GRID] The blade's grid header shows columns Image, Product, SKU, In stock quantity, Reserved quantity {OBSERVED}
[DOM] An "In stock only" filter checkbox is present and checked by default {OBSERVED}
[GRID] At least one row is rendered (grid is not stuck in a loading/error state) {SPEC}
Cross-layer: [API] The per-FFC products list is consistent with GET {{BACK_URL}}/api/inventory/fulfillmentcenters/@td(FC_EAST.id)/products (or the module's equivalent inventory-search endpoint) for the same FFC
[CONSOLE] No JS errors in the Admin SPA console while the blade loads
[NETWORK] No 4xx/5xx while opening the fulfillment center or Products blades
Failure signals: Products tab/widget missing or unresponsive; blade opens but never leaves a loading spinner; blade throws a JS error instead of rendering a grid; blade title does not match the selected fulfillment center

[GRID] With "In stock only" checked, every visible row's "In stock quantity" value is greater than 0 — no zero-quantity row appears {OBSERVED}
[GRID] With "In stock only" unchecked, at least one additional row appears whose "In stock quantity" is 0, that was absent from the filtered view {SPEC}
[STATE] Re-checking "In stock only" removes the zero-quantity row(s) again, confirming the filter — not the underlying data — controls visibility {SPEC}
Cross-layer: [API] The filtered result set size is strictly less than or equal to the unfiltered result set size for the same FFC
[NETWORK] No 4xx/5xx on the filter-toggle requests
Failure signals: A zero-quantity item appears while "In stock only" is checked; unchecking the filter makes no difference to the row count; the total product count badge does not change between filtered/unfiltered views

[MATH] The "In stock quantity" shown in the per-FFC blade equals the quantity shown for the same FFC in the product's own Fulfillment centers widget {SPEC}
[STATE] Both surfaces identify the same fulfillment center by the same name {SPEC}
Cross-layer: [API] Both values ultimately resolve from the same inventory record for (productId, fulfillmentCenterId) — no divergent cache between the two Admin surfaces
[CONSOLE] No JS errors while opening either widget
Failure signals: The two surfaces disagree on quantity for the same product+FFC pair; one surface shows stale data after a change made via the other (would require a follow-up write case, out of scope here — flag as observed only)

[GRID] Observation 1 (variation page): the row with SKU @td(INV_VARIATION_STOCKED.sku) shows In stock quantity @td(INV_VARIATION_STOCKED.stock) and its own Product Id — record all three {SPEC}
[GRID] Observation 2 (master page, a different page from Observation 1): the row with SKU @td(INV_VARIATION_MASTER.sku) shows In stock quantity @td(INV_VARIATION_MASTER.stock) and its own Product Id — record all three {SPEC}
[GRID] The two recorded Product Ids differ, confirming the variation is represented as its own distinct record and not folded into the master's row {SPEC}
[DOM] Observation 1's row displays the variation's own product name @td(INV_VARIATION_STOCKED.name), not a generic master-product label {SPEC}
Cross-layer: [API] The per-FFC products response includes the variation as its own list entry, keyed by Observation 1's recorded Product Id — not folded into the master product's entry
Failure signals: Only master/parent products are listed and variations are silently omitted; a variation row is present but shows the master product's name/SKU instead of its own; variation quantity is merged into the master's total; the two recorded Product Ids are identical
Guard note: this fulfillment center carries roughly 1,864 pre-existing orphaned inventory rows ("There is no product item with this ID", blank SKU — unrelated products deleted from the environment, not caused by this fixture). No assertion in this case may be phrased in terms of row counts or total page counts — both are unstable and unrelated to what this case proves.

[DOM] The grid area renders a "No data" placeholder — not a blank/white blade and not a JS error {OBSERVED}
[DOM] The "In stock only" filter checkbox is still present and interactive alongside the empty state {OBSERVED}
[BLADE] The blade title still shows the fulfillment center's name (e.g. @td(FC_INACTIVE.name)) {OBSERVED}
Cross-layer: [CONSOLE] No JS errors in the Admin SPA console for the zero-product FFC
[NETWORK] The underlying products request returns HTTP 200 with an empty result set — not a 4xx/5xx
Failure signals: Blank/white blade with no "No data" indicator; a JS error thrown instead of an empty state; the blade never finishes loading (infinite spinner); an error toast is shown for a legitimately empty FFC
